{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1356326-system-hack-simplified-spellcasting","id":1356326,"title":"System Hack: simplified spellcasting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-21T10:41:35-08:00","id":1356326,"title":"System Hack: simplified spellcasting","content":"NOTE: This is an attempt to make the math simpler for spellcasting, primarily by ditching primary spell factors. While it could be tweaked to not weaken arcana ratings and strengthen gnosis and yantras, that would remove the desired simplicity.<br /> <br /> So the basic concept of this hack is to invert &quot;-2 dice = +1 spell factor&quot; by making spell factor increases into the fundamental basis instead of dice, and probability of success (aka dicepool) into just another spell factor.<br /> <br /> <br /> When casting a spell you get Spell Points equal to Gnosis + Arcana + 1 per yantra.<br /> High quality or highly thematic yantras give +2 instead.<br /> Tripling ritual length give +1 Spell Point. Ritual length X 5 gives +2 Spell points instead<br /> <br /> Spell factor increases (as in going up one step on the chart of a given factor) cost 1 Spell Point<br /> Combined Spells cost 1 Spell Point per additional spell<br /> Unspent Spell Points do nothing.<br /> Primary spell factors don't exist<br /> <br /> Chance of Success starts off with 0 dice (aka a chance die) and adds +2 dice per Spell Point spent on it<br /> Circumstantial dice penalties and bonuses get applied to the dice pool made by the Chance of Success as normal","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3642,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","user":"Lareath","date":". 12-21-2019, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","name":"Lareath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T19:22:54-08:00","id":1356881,"title":"","content":"So now instead of adding and subtracting from one pool, you're subtracting from one pool (Spell points) and adding to another (Dice pool)? This doesn't seem less complex to me. Ymmv.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T20:21:56-08:00","id":1356893,"title":"","content":"I don't really see how this is simpler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-25T05:58:19-08:00","id":1356919,"title":"","content":"This seems more complex. You can say that the base casting pool starts at Gnosis + Arcanum, with spell factors costing 1 dice rather than 2. Yantras give 1 or more factors rather than the traditional 1/2, with great yantras giving a big +2 spell points, even if not a sacrament. <br /> <br /> The new system gives you the extra job of allocating factors every time, creating more complexity where the primary factor was automatically added. Spell factors are cheaper, yantras more powerful. This new system gives mages an incentive to depend on tools. However, the cheap spell factors also means less dependency on said tools. So in the end both systems seem at odds with each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 12-25-2019, 09:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 20